/-!
# Nondegenerate constant orbits of small autonomous Hamiltonians on manifolds

Let `σ` be a nondegenerate two-form on a manifold `M`, for instance the symplectic form of a closed
symplectic manifold, and `F : M → ℝ` a smooth function. A critical point `p` of `F` is a zero of
the Hamiltonian vector field `X_F`, so it is a constant 1-periodic orbit of every autonomous
Hamiltonian `ε F`. This file shows that for a Morse function and small `ε > 0` these constant
orbits are nondegenerate, which is the manifold form of
`TauCeti.Geometry.Symplectic.Hamiltonian.ConstantOrbit`.

Read `X_F` in the preferred chart at a critical point `p`, and let `L` be the derivative of its
coordinate expression at the chart image of `p`, the linearization of `X_F` at `p`. Differentiating
`dF(Y) = σ(X_F, Y)` at `p` along a vector field `Y`, the term carrying the derivative of `Y`
vanishes since `X_F(p) = 0`, so the critical Hessian of `F` is

`Hess F (p) (w, u) = σ_p(L w, u)`

(`TauCeti.SmoothTwoForm.IsNondegenerate.criticalHessian_apply_eq_eval₂_fderiv`). As `σ_p` is
nondegenerate, `L` is injective exactly when `p` is a nondegenerate critical point
(`injective_fderiv_mpullbackWithin_hamiltonianVectorField_iff`, in the namespace
`TauCeti.SmoothTwoForm.IsNondegenerate`). By the linearization of a flow at a rest point
(`TauCeti.eventually_isNondegenerateFixedPt_flowOf`), a nondegenerate critical point is then a
nondegenerate fixed point of the time-`t` map of `X_F` for every small `t ≠ 0`.

On a compact manifold the time-one map of `ε F` is the time-`ε` map of `X_F`
(`timeDependentFlowOf_hamiltonianVectorField_smul`). A Morse function on a compact manifold has
finitely many critical points, and for small `ε > 0` the 1-periodic orbits of `ε F` are exactly the
constant orbits at these points
(`exists_pos_forall_periodicSolutions_hamiltonianVectorField_smul_eq_image_criticalPoints`).
Together these give the main theorem
(`exists_pos_forall_isNondegenerateFixedPt_timeDependentFlowOf_smul`): for every Morse function `F`
on a closed manifold there is `ε₀ > 0` such that for `0 < ε ≤ ε₀` every 1-periodic orbit of `ε F`
is nondegenerate. Such `ε F` are thus admissible Hamiltonians for the Floer complex, generated by
the critical points of `F`.

## Main results

In the namespace `TauCeti.SmoothTwoForm.IsNondegenerate`:

* `criticalHessian_apply_eq_eval₂_fderiv`: at a critical point, the critical Hessian is `σ_p`
  applied to the linearization of the Hamiltonian vector field.
* `injective_fderiv_mpullbackWithin_hamiltonianVectorField_iff`: the linearization of `X_F` at a
  critical point is injective exactly when the critical point is nondegenerate.
* `eventually_isNondegenerateFixedPt_flowOf_hamiltonianVectorField`: a nondegenerate critical point
  is a nondegenerate fixed point of the time-`t` maps of `X_F` for small `t ≠ 0`.
* `timeDependentFlowOf_hamiltonianVectorField_smul`: on a compact manifold the flow of `ε F` from
  time `s` to time `t` is the time-`(t - s) * ε` map of `X_F`.
* `exists_pos_forall_isNondegenerateFixedPt_timeDependentFlowOf_smul`: for a Morse function `F` on
  a compact manifold, every 1-periodic orbit of `ε F` is nondegenerate for small `ε > 0`.

## References

* D. Salamon, *Lectures on Floer homology*, in *Symplectic geometry and topology*, IAS/Park City
  Math. Ser. 7 (1999), Lecture 1 (the Hamiltonian `ε H` of a Morse function `H`).
* D. McDuff, D. Salamon, *J-holomorphic curves and symplectic topology*, 2nd ed., AMS Colloquium
  Publications 52, 2012, Section 12.1 (the `C²`-small Morse Hamiltonians of the PSS comparison).
-/

public section

open Filter Function Set
open scoped Manifold Topology ContDiff

namespace TauCeti.SmoothTwoForm.IsNondegenerate

variable {E H M : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E]
  [TopologicalSpace H] {I : ModelWithCorners ℝ E H} [I.Boundaryless] [TopologicalSpace M]
  [ChartedSpace H M] [IsManifold I ∞ M] {σ : SmoothTwoForm I M} {F : M → ℝ} {p : M}

/-- **The Hessian at a critical point through the Hamiltonian vector field.** Let `σ` be a
nondegenerate two-form on a boundaryless finite-dimensional manifold, `F` a `C²` function and `p`
a critical point of `F`. Let `L` be the derivative at the chart image of `p` of the coordinate
expression of `X_F` in the preferred chart at `p`. Then `Hess F (p) (w, u) = σ_p(L w, u)`. -/
theorem criticalHessian_apply_eq_eval₂_fderiv (h : σ.IsNondegenerate)
    (hF : ContMDiff I 𝓘(ℝ) 2 F) (hcrit : mvfderiv I F p = 0) (w u : TangentSpace I p) :
    criticalHessian I F p w u = SmoothBundleForm.eval₂ σ p
      (fderiv ℝ (VectorField.mpullbackWithin 𝓘(ℝ, E) I (extChartAt I p).symm
        (σ.hamiltonianVectorField F) (range I)) (extChartAt I p p) w) u := by
  -- Extend `u` to a vector field `Y` and pair it with `X_F`; read both fields in the chart at `p`.
  let Y : (y : M) → TangentSpace I y := FiberBundle.extend E u
  let W : Fin 2 → (y : M) → TangentSpace I y := ![σ.hamiltonianVectorField F, Y]
  let V : Fin 2 → E → E := fun i ↦
    VectorField.mpullbackWithin 𝓘(ℝ, E) I (extChartAt I p).symm (W i) (range I)
  have hY : MDifferentiableAt I I.tangent (fun y ↦ (Y y : TangentBundle I M)) p :=
    FiberBundle.mdifferentiableAt_extend I E u
  have hYp : Y p = u := FiberBundle.extend_apply_self E u
  have hV : ∀ i, DifferentiableAt ℝ (V i) (extChartAt I p p) := fun i ↦ by
    have hW : MDifferentiableAt I I.tangent (fun y ↦ (W i y : TangentBundle I M)) p := by
      fin_cases i
      exacts [h.mdifferentiable_hamiltonianVectorField hF p, hY]
    have hd := MDifferentiableWithinAt.differentiableWithinAt_mpullbackWithin_extChartAt_symm
      (hW.mdifferentiableWithinAt (s := univ))
    rw [preimage_univ, univ_inter] at hd
    exact hd.differentiableAt (by rw [I.range_eq_univ]; exact univ_mem)
  have hσ : DifferentiableAt ℝ (RoughForm.inChartAt σ.1 p) (extChartAt I p p) :=
    RoughForm.differentiableAt_inChartAt σ.1 ((σ.contMDiff p).mdifferentiableAt (by simp))
  -- The Hessian against `Y p = u` is the derivative of `dF(Y) = σ(X_F, Y)`.
  have h1 := criticalHessian_apply_eq_mvfderiv (hF p) hcrit hY w
  rw [hYp] at h1
  have h2 : (fun y ↦ mvfderiv I F y (Y y)) = fun y ↦ σ.1 y (W · y) := by
    funext y
    rw [← h.apply_hamiltonianVectorField F y (Y y)]
    congr 1
    funext i
    fin_cases i <;> rfl
  -- That derivative is the derivative of the coordinate expression of `σ(X_F, Y)`.
  have h3 := fderivWithin_inChartAt_apply_mpullbackWithin (s := univ) (x := p) σ.1 W
    hσ.differentiableWithinAt (fun i ↦ (hV i).differentiableWithinAt)
  rw [mvfderivWithin_univ, preimage_univ, univ_inter,
    fderivWithin_of_mem_nhds (by rw [I.range_eq_univ]; exact univ_mem)] at h3
  have hV0 : V 0 (extChartAt I p p) = 0 := by
    simp only [V, W, Matrix.cons_val_zero]
    rw [VectorField.mpullbackWithin_extChartAt_symm_self]
    exact h.hamiltonianVectorField_eq_zero_iff.2 hcrit
  have hV1 : V 1 (extChartAt I p p) = u := by
    simp only [V, W, Matrix.cons_val_one, Matrix.cons_val_fin_one]
    rw [VectorField.mpullbackWithin_extChartAt_symm_self]
    exact hYp
  rw [h1, h2, ← h3]
  refine (fderiv_continuousAlternatingMap_apply_apply_of_eq_zero (g := V) hσ hV hV0 w).trans ?_
  have hupd : update (V · (extChartAt I p p)) 0 (fderiv ℝ (V 0) (extChartAt I p p) w) =
      ![fderiv ℝ (V 0) (extChartAt I p p) w, u] := by
    funext i
    fin_cases i
    · simp
    · simpa using hV1
  rw [hupd, RoughForm.inChartAt_extChartAt_self]
  exact (SmoothBundleForm.eval₂_apply σ p _ u).symm

/-- **Nondegenerate critical points are the zeros of `X_F` with injective linearization.** For a
nondegenerate two-form `σ` and a `C²` function `F` with a critical point `p`, the derivative at the
chart image of `p` of the coordinate expression of `X_F` in the preferred chart at `p` is injective
exactly when `p` is a nondegenerate critical point of `F`. -/
theorem injective_fderiv_mpullbackWithin_hamiltonianVectorField_iff (h : σ.IsNondegenerate)
    (hF : ContMDiff I 𝓘(ℝ) 2 F) (hcrit : mvfderiv I F p = 0) :
    Injective (fderiv ℝ (VectorField.mpullbackWithin 𝓘(ℝ, E) I (extChartAt I p).symm
        (σ.hamiltonianVectorField F) (range I)) (extChartAt I p p)) ↔
      IsManifoldNondegenerateCriticalPoint I F p := by
  set L := fderiv ℝ (VectorField.mpullbackWithin 𝓘(ℝ, E) I (extChartAt I p).symm
    (σ.hamiltonianVectorField F) (range I)) (extChartAt I p p)
  -- The critical Hessian and `L` have the same kernel, since `σ_p` is nondegenerate.
  have hker (w : TangentSpace I p) : criticalHessian I F p w = 0 ↔ L w = 0 := by
    refine ⟨fun hw ↦ isNondegenerate_iff_separatingLeft.1 h p (L w) fun u ↦ ?_, fun hw ↦ ?_⟩
    · rw [← criticalHessian_apply_eq_eval₂_fderiv h hF hcrit, hw]
      rfl
    · ext u
      rw [criticalHessian_apply_eq_eval₂_fderiv h hF hcrit, hw]
      exact (SmoothBundleForm.eval₂_apply σ p 0 u).trans
        ((σ.1 p).map_coord_zero (m := ![0, u]) 0 rfl)
  rw [isManifoldNondegenerateCriticalPoint_iff_criticalHessian]
  -- `L` acts on `E` and the critical Hessian on `TangentSpace I p`, which is `E` by definition.
  refine ⟨fun hL ↦ ⟨hF p, hcrit, criticalHessian_isInvertible_of_injective
      ((injective_iff_map_eq_zero _).2 fun w hw ↦ hL (((hker w).1 hw).trans (map_zero L).symm))⟩,
    ?_⟩
  rintro ⟨-, -, hinv⟩
  exact (injective_iff_map_eq_zero L).2 fun w hw ↦
    (injective_iff_map_eq_zero _).1 hinv.injective w ((hker w).2 hw)

variable [T2Space M]

/-- **Nondegenerate critical points are nondegenerate fixed points of the short-time maps.** For a
nondegenerate two-form `σ`, a `C³` function `F` and a nondegenerate critical point `p` of `F`, the
point `p` is a nondegenerate fixed point of the time-`t` map of `X_F` for every `t ≠ 0` close to
`0`. -/
theorem eventually_isNondegenerateFixedPt_flowOf_hamiltonianVectorField (h : σ.IsNondegenerate)
    (hF : ContMDiff I 𝓘(ℝ) 3 F) (hp : IsManifoldNondegenerateCriticalPoint I F p) :
    ∀ᶠ t in 𝓝[≠] 0, IsNondegenerateFixedPt I (flowOf (σ.hamiltonianVectorField F) t) p := by
  have hF2 : ContMDiff I 𝓘(ℝ) 2 F := hF.of_le (by norm_num)
  have hcrit := (isManifoldNondegenerateCriticalPoint_iff_criticalHessian.1 hp).2.1
  exact eventually_isNondegenerateFixedPt_flowOf
    (h.contMDiff_hamiltonianVectorField (n := 2) (by simp) (hF.of_le (by norm_num)))
    (h.hamiltonianVectorField_eq_zero_iff.2 hcrit)
    ((injective_fderiv_mpullbackWithin_hamiltonianVectorField_iff h hF2 hcrit).2 hp)

/-- **The flow of `ε F` is a rescaled flow of `X_F`.** On a compact manifold with a nondegenerate
two-form, for a `C²` function `F` and all `ε s t`, flowing the autonomous Hamiltonian `ε F` from
time `s` to time `t` is the time-`(t - s) * ε` map of the Hamiltonian vector field of `F`. -/
theorem timeDependentFlowOf_hamiltonianVectorField_smul [CompactSpace M] (h : σ.IsNondegenerate)
    (hF : ContMDiff I 𝓘(ℝ) 2 F) (ε s t : ℝ) :
    timeDependentFlowOf (fun _ ↦ σ.hamiltonianVectorField (ε • F)) s t =
      flowOf (σ.hamiltonianVectorField F) ((t - s) * ε) := by
  have hv : CMDiff 1 (fun y ↦ (⟨y, σ.hamiltonianVectorField F y⟩ : TangentBundle I M)) :=
    h.contMDiff_hamiltonianVectorField (n := 1) (by simp) (hF.of_le (by norm_num))
  have hεF : σ.hamiltonianVectorField (ε • F) = ε • σ.hamiltonianVectorField F :=
    funext (hamiltonianVectorField_const_smul ε)
  rw [hεF]
  exact timeDependentFlowOf_const_smul hv (isCompleteVectorField_of_compactSpace hv) ε s t

/-- **Small multiples of a Morse function have nondegenerate 1-periodic orbits.** Let `σ` be a
nondegenerate two-form on a compact boundaryless manifold modelled on a finite-dimensional space,
and `F` a Morse function. There is `ε₀ > 0` such that for `0 < ε ≤ ε₀` every 1-periodic orbit `γ`
of the autonomous Hamiltonian `ε F` is nondegenerate: `γ 0` is a nondegenerate fixed point of the
time-one map `timeDependentFlowOf X_{ε F} 0 1`. These orbits are the constant orbits at the
critical points of `F`. -/
theorem exists_pos_forall_isNondegenerateFixedPt_timeDependentFlowOf_smul [CompactSpace M]
    (h : σ.IsNondegenerate) (hF : IsMorse I F) :
    ∃ ε₀ > (0 : ℝ), ∀ ε, 0 < ε → ε ≤ ε₀ →
      ∀ γ ∈ periodicSolutions (fun _ ↦ σ.hamiltonianVectorField (ε • F)) 1,
        IsNondegenerateFixedPt I
          (timeDependentFlowOf (fun _ ↦ σ.hamiltonianVectorField (ε • F)) 0 1) (γ 0) := by
  have hFs : ContMDiff I 𝓘(ℝ) ∞ F := hF.contMDiff
  have hF2 : ContMDiff I 𝓘(ℝ) 2 F := hFs.of_le (by norm_num)
  obtain ⟨ε₀, hε₀, hper⟩ :=
    h.exists_pos_forall_periodicSolutions_hamiltonianVectorField_smul_eq_image_criticalPoints hF2
  -- Each of the finitely many critical points is nondegenerate for all small positive times.
  have hev : ∀ᶠ t in 𝓝[>] (0 : ℝ), ∀ q ∈ criticalPoints I F,
      IsNondegenerateFixedPt I (flowOf (σ.hamiltonianVectorField F) t) q := by
    refine hF.finite_criticalPoints.eventually_all.2 fun q hq ↦ ?_
    refine nhdsWithin_mono _ (fun t ht ↦ ne_of_gt ht)
      (h.eventually_isNondegenerateFixedPt_flowOf_hamiltonianVectorField
        (hFs.of_le (by norm_num))
        (hF.isManifoldNondegenerateCriticalPoint_of_mem_criticalPoints hq))
  obtain ⟨ε₁, hε₁, hsub⟩ := mem_nhdsGT_iff_exists_Ioo_subset.1 hev
  refine ⟨min ε₀ (ε₁ / 2), lt_min hε₀ (half_pos hε₁), fun ε hε hεle γ hγ ↦ ?_⟩
  rw [hper ε hε (hεle.trans (min_le_left _ _))] at hγ
  obtain ⟨q, hq, rfl⟩ := hγ
  rw [h.timeDependentFlowOf_hamiltonianVectorField_smul hF2 ε 0 1, sub_zero, one_mul]
  exact hsub ⟨hε, by linarith [min_le_right ε₀ (ε₁ / 2)]⟩ q hq

end TauCeti.SmoothTwoForm.IsNondegenerate
